    tags: [linter, embeds]
    text: >-
      **The HMD007 check follows only the embedded region** — it walks the
      section a fragment expands to, not every embed in the target card, so two
      embeds of different sections of one card, or a section embedding a sibling
      section, are no longer a false cycle. A card or a section that embeds
      itself still is. Held by the `embed-sections-of-one-card` and `embed-self`
      corpus cases; released in 0.5.0.
  - kind: done
    tags: [resolver]
    text: >-
      **The corrected resolution algorithm** — `..` is normalised in every form,
      leaving the namespace is HMD003 in every phase (a nested vault and a
      symbolic link out of the root included), a written card extension is
      honoured in every phase, a named import of another extension falls
      through, `[[./]]` and `[[../]]` reach only folder notes, every imported
      search path is probed so HMD016 names each shadowed card once, and HMD012
      is a warning. The eighteen `resolve-*` corpus cases, written from the
      specification, stand behind it; released in 0.5.0 [issue 0020].
  - kind: done
    tags: [language]
    text: >-
      **The HyperMarkDown 0.1 rules** — heading fragments match by key, so
      headings in every script are linkable [issue 0014], setext headings are
      headings, HMD019 reports undecodable files, a byte-order mark is ignored,
      all three line endings are lines, names compare after NFC (import aliases
      included), offsets count UTF-8 bytes and columns code points, only `.hmd/`
      marks a vault, an anchor on a heading embeds its section, an anchored
      repeat heading is not HMD011, and block anchors are no longer rendered —
      the tutorial's "you cannot see it" paragraph showed its own. A determinism
      test and six corpus cases stand behind it; released in 0.5.0.
  - kind: done
    tags: [site]
    text: >-
