    text: >-
      Does pruning the abandoned PyPI project mean yanking its releases or
      deleting it? Deletion frees the name for anyone to register and serve to a
      stale pin
    refs: >-
      [[hmd-0005#the-python-distribution-its-module-and-the-project-left-behind]]
  - kind: question
    tags: [domain]
    text: >-
      Does the retired domain redirect permanently, or for a fixed window after
      which the registration is allowed to lapse? A lapsed domain that once
      served documentation is one someone else can serve anything from
    refs: >-
      [[hmd-0005#the-canonical-host-and-the-state-dns-has-to-reach]]
  - kind: question
    tags: [cli]
    text: >-
      Should `hmd init` write a starter card in the root it creates? It creates
      an empty directory today, which lints clean and shows an author nothing —
      but a card written by a tool is a card somebody has to delete
    refs: >-
      [[hmd-0001#7-hmd-cli]]
  - kind: question
    tags: [cli, config]
    text: >-
      Should `init` grow flags for the settings it writes, or is editing the
      file it just wrote the right affordance?
    refs: >-
      [[hmd-0001#7-hmd-cli]]
  - kind: question
    tags: [linter, config]
    text: >-
      Should the linter check a namespace name that does not match the address
      form? Nothing reads that key yet, and the first thing to read it would be
      the first thing to break
    refs: >-
      [[hmd-0004#the-address-form]]
  - kind: question
    tags: [tests, language]
    text: >-
      Should the specification's version sentence stop being what the repository
      guard parses, now that a rename has shown the sentence can move?
    refs: >-
      [[hmd-0005#the-wiki-card-that-carries-the-project-s-name]]
