| todo    | **An embedded card's Markdown links resolve from the host page.** Expansion is textual and carries a wikilink back to the card it was written in, but an ordinary relative link is plain text to it and is resolved from the page that embeds it                           | A link, an image, or a path to a card written in an embedded card is wrong on every host in another directory, on the site and in `hmd render`. MkDocs reports it at `info` only, so a strict build stays green                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | site, embeds    | [the issue card](../issues/0012-embedded-markdown-links-resolve-from-the-host-page.hmd), [[hmd-0001#6-embed-expansion]] |
| blocked | **The retired domain answers 404 instead of redirecting.** Its records point at a forwarding service, so the registrar side is half-configured, but no rule takes effect on either scheme                                                                                  | Every link published under the old host is dead. The fix is a web form, not a commit                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | domain          | [[hmd-0005#the-canonical-host-and-the-state-dns-has-to-reach]]                                                          |
| todo    | **A heading that ends in a code span loses that span.** The scanner measures where a heading ends on the masked text, in which inline code is blank, so code at the end of a heading is cut off before the heading's text is read. Code in the middle of a heading is kept | A reference to the proposal heading *4. Red links and .md*, whose last word is a code span, is reported as a missing heading (HMD004) unless the fragment leaves that word out. A tracker titled *STATUS* followed by a code span is reported as a duplicate of its own *Status* section (HMD011). Five tracker references are written without their last word so that the linter passes: `#4-red-links-and` in four places and `#the-divergence-with` in one. They must gain the word back when this is fixed, and the linter will report them then | linter, scanner | [[hmd-lang-spec#heading-anchors]]                                                                                       |
| todo    | **A code span that contains three backticks opens a fenced region.** A span written with single backticks around three backticks is read as the start of a fence, which runs to the next such span, across paragraphs                                                      | Between two such spans, a wikilink shown inside a code span is read as a real wikilink and reported as unresolved (HMD001). Found in the requirements sketch under `doc/models/`, which now writes those two spans with character references                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | linter, scanner | [[hmd-lang-spec#lexical-model]]                                                                                         |
