| map(r => { Shipped: r.text, Tags: r.tags | join(", ") })
| Table(columns = ["Shipped", "Tags"])
| format(as = Markdown)
```
<!-- hql:output hash=f0400f06f960 status=ok -->
| Shipped                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             | Tags            |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------- |
| **"Vault not found" when no `.hmd/` is above the start directory** — the error reads the way git's does outside a repository and says to run `hmd init` or pass `--root`; the README no longer describes the `wiki` setting or the `--wiki` flag; released in 0.5.1                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | config, cli     |
| **`location_path` names the namespace root** — the setting formerly called `wiki`, read relative to the vault with the default `.`, the vault itself, instead of `doc/wiki`; no alias. `hmd init --location-path` replaces `--wiki`, and with no flag creates no directory; released in 0.5.0.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | config          |
| **The HMD007 check follows only the embedded region** — it walks the section a fragment expands to, not every embed in the target card, so two embeds of different sections of one card, or a section embedding a sibling section, are no longer a false cycle. A card or a section that embeds itself still is. Held by the `embed-sections-of-one-card` and `embed-self` corpus cases; released in 0.5.0.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | linter, embeds  |
| **The corrected resolution algorithm** — `..` is normalised in every form, leaving the namespace is HMD003 in every phase (a nested vault and a symbolic link out of the root included), a written card extension is honoured in every phase, a named import of another extension falls through, `[[./]]` and `[[../]]` reach only folder notes, every imported search path is probed so HMD016 names each shadowed card once, and HMD012 is a warning. The eighteen `resolve-*` corpus cases, written from the specification, stand behind it; released in 0.5.0 [issue 0020].                                                                                     | resolver        |
| **The HyperMarkDown 0.1 rules** — heading fragments match by key, so headings in every script are linkable [issue 0014], setext headings are headings, HMD019 reports undecodable files, a byte-order mark is ignored, all three line endings are lines, names compare after NFC (import aliases included), offsets count UTF-8 bytes and columns code points, only `.hmd/` marks a vault, an anchor on a heading embeds its section, an anchored repeat heading is not HMD011, and block anchors are no longer rendered — the tutorial's "you cannot see it" paragraph showed its own. A determinism test and six corpus cases stand behind it; released in 0.5.0. | language        |
| **A syntax highlighter for cards** — a code sample marked `hmd` is coloured as a card wherever Pygments is used: links, embeds, block anchors, and frontmatter stand out, and a fenced block inside the sample is coloured as its own language.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     | site            |
| **The format, entire** — masking and the link grammar, heading links rewritten to the id Python-Markdown's table of contents gives the heading they matched, so links and rendered anchors cannot disagree, the four-phase resolution search — named imports, the spine, imported search paths, then the whole-tree sweep — folder notes, both import forms, and embed expansion with a depth cap and cycle detection.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | language        |
| **Markdown cards** — `.md` and `.markdown` files load as cards that are not scanned, bind after `.hmd`, and are reported as HMD018 when shadowed; the MkDocs plugin links to the page MkDocs builds from one and never registers it; a heading right below the frontmatter fence is a heading again [HMD-0029].                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     | language        |
| **`hmd lint`** — nineteen diagnostics with stable identifiers, JSON output, and exit codes a CI job can read.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | cli, linter     |
| **`hmd render`** — flat markdown and HTML.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | cli             |
| **`hmd init`** — writes the project marker with every setting at its default, creates the namespace root it names, refuses to overwrite an existing config, and warns when an enclosing project would silently win.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | cli, config     |
| **The `[hql]` and `[semantics]` tables are left alone** — a configuration holding them loads and lints as one without them, whatever their values, and a test holds that [[hmd-0028#the-hql-table]].                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | config          |
| **The MkDocs plugin** — cards become pages, folder notes collapse onto their directory's URL, links are rewritten, red links render as red links without failing the build, embeds expand, and diagrams render through `d2`.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | site            |
| **Publication** — opt-in visibility inherited from folder notes, unpublished cards absent from the built site entirely, and a warning when a published card reaches into one that is not.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | site            |
| **Released and renamed** — on PyPI through a trusted publisher, under a name that now matches the domain, the npm scope, and the extension publisher, with the old entry point kept working as an alias.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            | package, rename |
| **The repository layout** — five tools under `tools/`, each owning its own front matter with no packaging symlinks, the shared corpus at the root where it belongs to every implementation, and a workspace root that is not itself a package.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | package         |
| **A nested vault is its own vault** — a directory below the root carrying its own `.hmd/` is skipped when the workspace loads, so linting, the graph, rendering, and the site see none of its cards, and an import into it is HMD015. Ships in 0.3.1 [issue 0009]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | resolver        |
| **A folder note's ordinary links land on the built site** — the plugin registers a folder note one directory above its file, and now resolves every relative Markdown link in it from the file's own directory before rewriting it for the registered page: links to cards, to plain pages, and to images, inline and as reference definitions. Ships in 0.3.1 [issue 0010]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | site            |
| **The shared corpus runs here too** — every conformance case is checked against this implementation, the TypeScript one, and the Rust crate, so drift is caught whichever side moves. This one carries no expected-failure ledger, and its expected results are written from the specification, not generated from this code.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | tests           |
